.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_BAND_EDGE "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_band_edge (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_band_edge \- tabulate material parameters for heterostructure.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_band_edge
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find band\-edge parameters for a heterostructure
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.TP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-mass\fR ] arg
Set a constant effective\-mass across the
structure (relative to free electron).
If not specified, the mass is calculated
automatically for all positions in the
material.
.TP
\fB\-M\fR [ \fB\-\-material\fR ] arg (=gaalas)
Material ID: "gaalas" for
Ga(1\-x)Al(x)As, "cdmnte" for
Cd(1\-x)Mn(x)Te, or "inalgaas" for
In(1\-x\-y)Al(x)Ga(y)As
.TP
\fB\-p\fR [ \fB\-\-particle\fR ] arg (=e)
Particle to be used: 'e', 'h' or 'l'
.HP
\fB\-\-dcpermittivityfile\fR arg (=eps_dc.r) File containing the dc permittivity
.TP
\fB\-\-alloyfile\fR arg (=x.r)
File from which alloy is read
.TP
\fB\-\-bandedgepotentialfile\fR arg (=v_b.r) File to which band\-edge potential is
written
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files

    'x.r' Alloy composition:
          Column 1: Spatial location [m]
          Column 2: Alloy fraction (x)
          Column 3: Alloy fraction (y, optional)

For materials where the 2nd alloy component is not needed (E.g., AlGaAs), just omit the last column

.SS Output files

    'v_b.r'    Band-edge profile [J]
    'alpha.r'  Nonparabolicity parameter [1/J]
    'Eg.r'     Bandgap [J]
    'eps_dc.r' Low-frequency permittivity [F/m]
    'm.r'      Effective mass (in growth direction) [kg]
    'mperp.r'  Effective mass (perpendicular to growth direction) [kg]:
               Column 1: Spatial location [m]
               Column 2: Parameter (as listed above)
.SH EXAMPLES

Tabulate material properties for electrons in an GaAlAs system:
    qwwad_ef_band_edge --particle e --material gaalas

As above, but force the effective mass to 0.07 m0 throughout:
    qwwad_ef_band_edge --particle e --material gaalas --mass 0.07
